{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>That he give me the cave of Machpelah.</b> It is called Machpelah because the Holy One, blessed be He, doubled there the stature of the first man, and it had been called thus from eternity, but the Hittites did not know the reason why; nor did Ephron sell it with the knowledge that there was a tomb there. And what he said, 'that he give me,' and then said, 'let him give it to me' — that is, I shall consider it as though he gives it to me as a gift, but 'for full silver let him give it to me,' for Abraham would not ask for a gift but only for a purchase. Nor was he asking for the field but only for 'the cave that is at the edge of the field,' for that was enough for him for burial. And Ephron answered him in the way of courtesy: 'The field I have given you, and the cave that is in it,' for a man as honored as you — it is not fitting that the cave be yours while the field belongs to another; rather, 'I give it all to you as a gift, the field and the cave.' And the expression 'I have given' means in this case: it is as though I have given. And so Abraham answered him: 'I have given the silver of the field' — that is, I do not want a free gift but only that you sell it to me; and as for the payment, it is as though I have given."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:22.775152643Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}